        <p>Cheshire Subsidences —A Sinking Library. On Tuesday night,at a meeting of the Northwich Urban District Council, on the proposition of Mr Sutherst, it was decided to adopt the first part of the Museum and Gymnasiums Act, whereby a rate could be levied to permit certain necessary repairs being executed. It was explained that the institution was presented to the town by Sir John Brunner, and that its present condition through subsidence was dangerous and necessitated an expenditure of several hundred pounds. The walls were considerably out of plumb and there were large rents in'thein. It was not deemed advisable , to approach the donor for further pecuniary assist- ance.</p>
