        <p>If you find that your system is unable to bear the oppressive heat, and you are almost unable to fc:low your vocation, immediately strengthen your constitu- non by taking a course of Gwilym Evans' Quin:ne Bitters. This preparation makes the weak strong, and gives new heart and " go" to the weary toiler. It revives the spirits and strengthens the nerves, and by giving tone to the whole constitution, wards 4.ff fevers, and many other ailments prevalent at this time or the year. No family should be without a bottle in the hour. An occasional dose, taken when feeling slightly out of sorts, has prevented many a long illness. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is The Best Remedy of The Age for Weakness, Nervousness, Indigestion, LOW Spirits, Sleeplessness, Influenza, and Chest Affections. It is often asked, " How is it that one single medicine like Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is capable of curing so many aifferent diseases ?" The reply,trowever,is simple enough. Most diseases have a common source, either in a deranged stomach and its connections, or in weak and impure blood. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, by striking at the root of the evil, by strengthening the stomach and purifying, the blood, places these impor- tant life sources in proper working order, and the disease, under whatever form it may have shown itself, disappears: Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters is sold by all chemists and stores, in bottles 2s. 9d. and 4s.6.l.eaCh. Refuse to take substitutes.</p>
