        <p>On Tuesday, a bride and bridegroom and party suf- fered a sore disappointment at Fleetwood. A wedding had been arranged to take place at the Parish Church at half-past two, but at three o'clock no minister had put in an appearance, and messengers wbo had been despatched to the homes of the three clergymen re turned without finding one to tip the nuptial knot. rh. bride and bridegroom waited in vain for the perform' ance of the ceremony that would make them one, and at last had to re•urn to their respective homes in a state of single blessedoeSs. The good things provided for the wedding breakfast bad perforce to be laid aside.</p>
