        <p>William and Ellen Lillywhite, of Camellia-street, Wandsworth, were on Tuesday arresqed on the coroner's warrant for the manslaughter of their infant, who died from starvation accelerated by filthy surroundings. The man Richard Edward Goodall, of Archer-street' Camden Town, was at Marclebone further remanded on the charge of murdering his three children by throwing them inro the Regent's Canal ; and at the conclusion Pf the proceedings, Mr Curtis Bennett told the bray Con- strble Milne, who tried to save the children, that a lady had sent £1 in recognition of his conduct.</p>
